+The Point-Based Neural Renderer is a differentiable rendering module that projects a 3D point cloud and camera pose into a 2D feature map by splatting points and blending them via alpha-compositing [S1]. It enables end-to-end training by allowing photometric and perceptual loss gradients to propagate back to optimized point attributes (color, depth, normal, uncertainty, and latent features) and network weights [S1]. Unlike methods that rely on a single input image, this architecture requires fusing multiple input views and renders each point cloud individually at target viewpoints before fusion [S1].
 
